[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '90,932 tokens, 61,572 tokens. Same bug, same model, same fix. The only difference was one sentence in'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the prompt. Never hitting the codeex limit again comes down to 12 changes you make once. and I metered every one of them on that same broken button on GPT6 Astra on my'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'own account. Five of the 12 moved the meter. Three tips you\'ll hear everywhere failed it. One saved nothing. One is simply wrong about how Codex builds and'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'one cost me 13% more. Codex runs 2 meters at once, a 5-hour window and a weekly window. And you need room in both. The 5-hour window starts when you send your first message and it'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'runs for 5 hours from there. Messages are also weighted by model. On the $20 plan, Open AI\'s own table gives Astra roughly 5 to 45 messages per window and'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Luna 250 to 2,000. One Astra message costs about the same allowance as 50 Luna messages. Keep that number, it comes back. Rule one, open your config file and look'

[01:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for service tier. Mine said priority. That is the old name for fast mode renamed at the end of July. And fast mode uses about twice the allowance on every turn. If you did not choose that'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on purpose, delete the line and turn fast on only for the turns where you want it. Rule two. I sent a one-word reply on a clean install and then on my real setup with 17 plugins switched on. Clean'

[01:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '14,164 input tokens. Mine 19,040. That is 4,876 extra tokens on every turn. 34% before I had typed anything. If you did not turn'

[02:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a plug-in on for today\'s job, turn it off. Image generation is worse. Open a I says it burns the allowance three to five times faster than a normal message. Rule three, fix the buttons cost 90,932'

[02:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tokens on average. Fix the buttons. The handler is in toolbar.js. Clicking should set the body theme cost 61,572.'

[02:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '32% less in both runs and it finished in half the time. Codeex spends most of a small job looking for where to start. Two extra clauses in the prompt. Skip the search.'

[02:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Rule four, three lines in the project\'s agents file. Reply in three lines or fewer say only that a check passed. Give detail on failures. Output tokens dropped 28% from 1,173'

[02:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to 842 and the fix was identical. Ask for the long explanation when you want one. If this video is useful, hit subscribe'

[03:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'because it\'s free. And if you want to back the work, hit join here or the supporter button on Facebook. Now, the tips that failed. Rule five, Open AI\'s help page says to try Astra at low or medium before'

[03:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reaching for high and that higher effort does not always produce a better result. I believe them for reasoning heavy work on this bug. Low saved nothing. 99,000 tokens one run, 80,000 the next against'

[03:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a base of 90,000. My rule now is medium by default, high when the problem is genuinely hard, and low for questions where I only want an answer.'

[03:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Rule six, the tip going around is to tell Astra to finish the task inside a percentage of your weekly limit. I asked Astra in a fresh session whether it'

[03:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'could see how much of my allowance was left. It answered no. Then I added, "Use at most 2% of my weekly limit to the same bug prompt." Both runs came out 13% worse, 102,000 tokens against 90,000.'

[04:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The model cannot read your meter. Telling it to be careful just made it do more checking. Rule seven, same bug with Luna as the main model. 69,116'

[04:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tokens against 90,932, 24% fewer. and the fix passed both times. The token number underells it because a Luna message counts against'

[04:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your window at roughly a 50th of an Astra message. Let Astra plan hand the routine execution to Luna sub agents and have Astra review the result. Open AI\'s own docs warn that sub aents use more'

[04:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tokens in total. The allowance math is what makes it worth it. Rule eight. Because the 5-hour window starts on your first message, the time you send it matters. Schedule one automation that'

[05:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sends a single line at 6:00 in the morning. Now, your window resets at 11:00 while you\'re still on your first coffee instead of at 2:00 in the afternoon when you finally hit the wall.'

[05:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'On the $20 plan, this is the cheapest hour you will ever buy. Rule nine, your stack, your tone, how you want answers formatted. Put them in the global agents'

[05:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'file once instead of retyping them every session. Keep it short. Every bite in that file rides every turn and Codeex stops reading at 32 kilobytes without'

[05:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'telling you. Once a month, ask Codeex to review the file and remove anything duplicated or outdated. Rule 10. When a workflow works, save it as a skill. Codeex reads only the name'

[05:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and a oneline description at the start of a task and opens the full instructions when it decides to use that skill. So, a skill you don\'t need today costs almost nothing to keep.'

[06:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Rules 11 and 12. Set follow-up behavior to steer. A correction then lands while Codex is still working instead of after it finishes a job you were about to'

[06:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'throw away. And watch the context. Astra\'s window is a million tokens. But any request past 272,000 is built at double on every token. So set autoco compact around 200,000. Don\'t add or'

[06:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'remove tools in the middle of a long thread. That breaks the cache which now lasts 30 minutes. And for anything that runs over an hour, have Codeex keep a short progress file. So a crash does not mean paying for the same work twice.'

[06:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Resets. A bank reset refreshes both windows and there were two handed out at the Astra launch. Purchased resets exist in some countries. Neither changes how much a task costs, so fix the 12 first.'

